  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 PM EDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nPattern Synopsis/Forecast: Vertically stacked low pressure is in the \nprocess of crossing well to our north across Hudson Bay. Attendant \nweak cold front is draped from northern Quebec southwestward into \nthe central Plains -- slowly making inroads into the eastern U.P. \nThis boundary will work its way into northern lower by early evening \nand clear the area the forecast area to the southeast tonight. \nCouple of cooler days on tap Monday-Tuesday as a result, but \nnorthern MI should sit on the periphery of ~1035mb high pressure \npassing by to our north with little in the way of active weather to \nstart the work week. Focus then turns to the Wednesday night - \nThursday time frame as another wave treks out of the Pac NW \ninto north-central Canada, again dragging a cold front across \nnorthern MI. This period looks to feature higher rain shower \nchances locally. Additional more active weather may return for \nparts of the Halloween weekend.\n\nForecast Details: Cold front alluded to above is making headway into \neastern upper early this afternoon, expected to make slow southeast \nprogress into northern lower later this afternoon/early evening, \neventually clearing the forecast area late tonight. While impacts \nshould be nil, isolated to scattered light rain shower chances will \naccompany this boundary, primarily across the eastern U.P. this \nafternoon before gradually sagging south this evening through \ntonight. A few showers may linger across far southeast areas into \nearly Monday morning. All in all, not a lot of rain, with the vast \nmajority of the area hard-pressed to get more than a few hundredths, \nif any at all. \n\nPost-frontal cooler temperatures progged for Monday and Tuesday with \nhighs in the upper 40s far north and through the 50s over northern \nlower -- certainly closer to what would be considered normal for \nlate October.\n\nTemperatures rebound back to well-above normal levels Wednesday as \nnorthern MI sits firmly under WAA in advance of a wave trekking from \nthe northern Plains to near Hudson Bay. Highs Wednesday progged in \nthe 60s to near 70 area-wide. This warmth in advance of that system \ndragging another cold front across the area by late Wednesday night \ninto Thursday. Shower chances return through this time and currently \nexpected to be more numerous/widespread than today-tonight's \nshowers. \n\nLooking toward Halloween weekend, above normal temperatures \nanticipated for Friday through Sunday, with latest trends supporting \nlow-mid 60s over northern lower and a touch cooler north of the \nbridge for Halloween day. Rain chances may return next weekend as \nwell, but lots of spatial/temporal uncertainty at this point.",
